{"id": "EUVD-2026-101265", "enisaUuid": "d21db58e-f251-3ef3-98d3-3ebe4d41df9c", "description": "buildebooks before 0.2.2 contains an OS command injection vulnerability in lib/kindle.js that allows attackers to execute commands by supplying a crafted EPUB file name passed to kindlegen via child_process.exec. Attackers can craft a book project with a malicious front-matter filename or project folder name and kindle: true to execute OS commands as the user running buildebooks.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T14:17:09", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T18:16:18", "baseScore": 8.5, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/wastemobile/buildebooks/pull/12", "https://github.com/wastemobile/buildebooks/commit/123776c9ef61e8075ada2f7da2f7046f6a8078d9", "https://github.com/wastemobile/buildebooks/blob/7fc313485447d9359fb38fda3cbc2ed60ce69fe7/lib/kindle.js#L5-L12", "https://github.com/wastemobile/buildebooks", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/buildebooks-before-0.2.2-os-command-injection-via-kindlegen-epub-file-name"], "aliases": ["GHSA-xq9r-4xcp-j7fm", "CVE-2026-110637"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 1.15, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "352c7136-4d0f-3eed-b5ab-7ccd42d0c60c", "product": {"name": "buildebooks", "vendor": {"name": "wastemobile"}}, "product_version": "0 <0.2.2"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "85d86778-575e-3aa3-b155-e7daf7e929df", "vendor": {"name": "wastemobile"}}], "isExploited": false}